//
// The battery meter (design_handoff_panels `.meter`): a 6px groove with a
// green fill, in the Control Center's fixed 80px slot and again full-width in
// the Battery panel. The caller sizes the groove; the meter fills its share.
//
// It is a thin dress over `ProgressBar` rather than two flex boxes, because a
// modifier argument cannot be an expression — `.grow($props.percent)` reads as
// grow 0, silently. A widget PROP is the only place a value flows into layout,
// which is what makes `value:` the right seam for anything data-driven.

Component Meter {
    props: {
        percent: Int,
    }
    ProgressBar { value: $props.percent, height: 6 }
        .fg(success)
}
